      "review_description": "Ionics Energy do not warrant their product, we have had the system installed 18 months ago then the inverter stopped working. After numerous phone calls to Ionics Energy we only had 1 phone call returned and and a few emails to us with lies to us about the inverter was coming { and it didn't come} then they said they had to threaten a law suite to get the inverter which was coming after the threat { which didn't come} so after getting messed around for 10 weeks {yes 10 weeks}  i then called the company of the inverter and after a few phone calls to China  and a couple of emails they confirmed that a inverter was on its way which arrived in five days to my house in Cairns. They also said there was no warranty claim put in for the serial number of our inverter so it was all lies. We then got the inverter installed to no help of Ionics energy at all...http://ionics.com.au",
